---
---

<section id="why-konteks" class="py-20 md:py-28 bg-[#F8FAFC]">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12 lg:gap-16">

      <!-- Problems -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-7 space-y-10">
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="h-px w-6 bg-indigo-300"></span>
            <span class="font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-indigo-600">The problem</span>
          </span>
          <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 tracking-tight">
            Why do users have to repeat themselves?
          </h2>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-base sm:text-lg max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
            A conversation app works fine until you touch the stack. Then everything your
            product already knew about the user quietly disappears.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="divide-y divide-slate-200 border-t border-slate-200">

          <div class="py-8 flex gap-5">
            <div class="w-11 h-11 shrink-0 rounded-xl bg-amber-50 text-amber-600 flex items-center justify-center">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M21 12a9 9 0 1 1-9-9" />
                <path d="M21 3v6h-6" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1.5">Change anything and it forgets</h3>
              <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                New model, new framework, a redeploy, and the conversation starts from zero.
                Users get asked about things they already told it, in the same chat.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="py-8 flex gap-5">
            <div class="w-11 h-11 shrink-0 rounded-xl bg-indigo-50 text-indigo-600 flex items-center justify-center">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="6" rx="1.5" />
                <rect x="3" y="14" width="18" height="6" rx="1.5" />
                <path d="M7 7v.01M7 17v.01" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1.5">Every turn re-sends everything</h3>
              <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                The whole history goes in again on every single reply, most of it irrelevant.
                Slower responses, noisier prompts, higher costs.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="py-8 flex gap-5">
            <div class="w-11 h-11 shrink-0 rounded-xl bg-violet-50 text-violet-600 flex items-center justify-center">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M14.7 6.3a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.4l1.6 1.6a1 1 0 0 0 1.4 0l3.77-3.77a6 6 0 0 1-7.94 7.94l-6.91 6.91a2.12 2.12 0 0 1-3-3l6.91-6.91a6 6 0 0 1 7.94-7.94l-3.76 3.76z" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1.5">The plumbing is all yours</h3>
              <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Message storage, conversation state, summaries, memory, and retrieval. Every
                app rebuilds the same machinery by hand, then maintains it forever.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Solution -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-5">
        <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-24 bg-white border border-slate-200/80 rounded-2xl shadow-soft-indigo p-8 sm:p-10">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="h-px w-6 bg-emerald-300"></span>
            <span class="font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-emerald-700">The fix</span>
          </span>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 tracking-tight mt-5">
            Konteks keeps the story.
          </h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-3">
            One conversation, kept in one place, ready for every reply, no matter which
            frontend is answering.
          </p>

          <ul class="mt-8 space-y-5">
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 text-emerald-600 shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
              </svg>
              <div>
                <p class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">One room per conversation</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Messages, state, and summaries live together in one persistent place.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 text-emerald-600 shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
              </svg>
              <div>
                <p class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">Right context, right turn</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Just what this reply needs: what was said, what's decided, what matters.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 text-emerald-600 shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
              </svg>
              <div>
                <p class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">Survives any switch</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Swap models, frameworks, or frontends. The conversation keeps going.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>